      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Logging in after the update was quite overwhelming. I had HUD details set to full, and the HUD went from \"always-on mic icon\" to \"plenty cluttered\".\n\nI can't turn off the HUD without turning off the mic status and notification popups. If I want mic status, I can set the HUD opacity to 0, but that still hides the notifications. Such a frustrating change.\n\nHope this feedback gets seen",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-10-04T03:00:15.638Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, setting HUD opacity to 0 to hide the ESC and mic icons also hides notifications (invites, joins, group announcements). Please add independent controls, such as a toggle to hide the on-screen ESC/mic icons, or a separate opacity/visibility setting for notifications, so players can keep a clean view without losing real-time info.\n\nCome on, what the hell is going on with the design team? Why do I need an ESC Icon in the screen, or a clickable Mic Icon, if I have to press a key (ALT) to access it, WHEN pressing ESC already leads me to the Menu where the mic button actually is?\n\nThey're both ONE keypress of distance.\n\nIs VRChat targetting toddlers/elders gamers now? Because that's the only public I can imagine which wouldn't be able to know how to press ESC or how to mute/unmute themselves.\n\nSeriously, I need to lose access to actual real-time useful informations in order to make my UI clean again?",
